\section*{Universal strong Kadison–Kastler stability for von Neumann algebras}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For any prescribed small unitary displacement, the paper claims one uniform Kadison--Kastler tolerance guaranteeing conjugacy of close unital von Neumann algebras on any complex Hilbert space. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 289, 2026-09-23): For finite factors, free-word estimates control amplification while boundary averaging corrects nearby unitaries into a measurable cocycle. Double ergodicity makes the resulting correspondence multiplicative and yields a spatial implementation. Properly infinite algebras are handled through matrix amplification and modular preparation; alignment of centers and limits over separable restrictions assemble the universal conclusion.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 289, 2026-09-23): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 289, the scope page documents the following selections. The selection gives a tolerance depending only on the requested distance of an implementing unitary from identity, for two close common-identity von Neumann algebras. The separate one-way near-inclusion and general norm-closed examples are outside it. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: StrongKadisonKastler.lean. Declarations: OAI.KadisonKastler.universal\_strong\_stability.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

